{"labs": [{"stimuli": [{"id": 0, "contents": [{}], "template_override": 1, "type": "welcome", "_data": []}, {"id": 1, "contents": [{"value": {"audiosrc": "enpe7n1le01ob05re2aud01", "coverimg": "enpe7n1le01ob05re2img01.jpg", "images": [{"id": 0, "image": "enpe7n1le01ob05re2img01.jpg", "text": "<strong>Peter: </strong> Mr. Kumal can I talk to you? I want to make sure I am working on my project using the correct information. </br>\n<strong>Mr. Kumal: </strong> How can I help you?</br>\n<strong>Peter: </strong> First, you mentioned that when we are programming organization of words and symbols make any programming language usable, so we have to use programming comments. </br>\n<strong>Mr. Kumal: </strong> Exactly, continue, please.<br/>\n<strong>Peter: </strong> You mentioned syntax is a set of rules that can indicate the appropriate arrangement of words and symbols to structure a computer program. Thus, the programmers are always paying attention to logic and syntax because any minor error can represent a mess in execution. </br></br>", "time": "100"}, {"id": 1, "image": "enpe7n1le01ob05re2img02.jpg", "text": "<strong>Mr. Kumal: </strong> Yes, why don't we go straight to the point? </br>\n<strong>Peter: </strong> Ok teacher. Can you tell me about statements, variables, and keywords? </br>\n<strong>Mr. Kumal: </strong> Yes, syntax includes all of them; a statement is a simple unit of code established as an execution path. A variable can be a sign or a symbol that stores values like strings, numbers or Boolean values indicating an operation to perform. And the keywords are reserved commands with a specific meaning, when programmers are writing commands such as \u201cprint\u201d, \u201cimport\u201d or \u201cexport\u201d, in fact, they are using keywords. </br></br>", "time": "39500"}, {"id": 2, "image": "enpe7n1le01ob05re2img03.jpg", "text": "<strong>Peter: </strong> Teacher, why don't we discuss about controlling workflow? </br>\n<strong>Mr. Kumal: </strong> Yes, let me give you an example; programs are executed following steps but, what can you do when you need to skip a step? Imagine you go to an ATM machine to withdraw $100 if you have the correct balance, the machine gives you the money; but, if your balance is less than the requested amount, for sure you will see the message: \u201cinsufficient balance\u201d. That is the workflow path which is indicating how the program can skip a part of the code when necessary.", "time": "81000"}]}, "type": "slideshow"}], "title": "", "type": "audio", "template_override": 1, "_data": []}], "id": 0, "type": "scholar", "exercises": [{"id": 0, "img_path": "", "template_override": 1, "type": "WLC", "stimuli_ids": [0], "questions": [], "_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "I can talk about the concept of syntax in programming language. ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "I can present in an easy way concepts like statements, variables, and keywords.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "I can discuss an example to understand the concept of controlling workflows.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "Do you consider appropriate to organize commands when programming? Why?", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": "What are the most important aspects to execute codes of a computer program? Why?", "type": "Free Header Item"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Welcome", "type": "group_name"}], "type": "group"}, {"content": {"allowed_attempts": 2, "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "try again", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time", "type": "text"}], "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "You have 2 tries", "type": "text"}, {"content": "you have 1 attempt left", "type": "text"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct"}, "type": "feedback"}, {"content": "Ask your partner:", "type": "free_header_text"}, {"content": "Using Syntax to Structure a Program", "type": "free_type_text_area"}]}, {"id": 1, "template_override": 1, "type": "STI", "questions": [{"id": 0, "respons