ng important is missing.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time...", "type": "text"}], "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}, {"content": "", "type": "text"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct!"}, "type": "feedback"}]}, {"id": 12, "template_override": 1, "type": "DWS", "questions": [{"id": 0, "responses": [{"selected": 0, "id": 0, "correct": 1, "_data": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}]}], "_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "enpe7n1le01ob05re7pdf01.pdf", "type": "pdf"}], "type": "question"}]}], "stimuli_ids": [], "_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "Bringing statements examples to class", "type": "text"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Take Away", "type": "group_name"}], "type": "group"}, {"content": {"allowed_attempts": 2, "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "Whoops! Something important is missing.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time...", "type": "text"}], "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}, {"content": "", "type": "text"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct!"}, "type": "feedback"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Instructions: Complete the following steps. Fill in the Self-Assessment.", "type": "text"}], "type": "post_instructions"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Writing", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Speaking", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Reading", "type": "skill"}], "type": "learning_skills"}]}], "_data": [{"contents": [{"content": true, "type": "has_nav"}, {"content": true, "type": "has_exercise_controls"}], "type": "lab_options"}]}], "type": "sena", "_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Programming Logic and Syntax ", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 5, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 1, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "A1.1", "type": "level"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"content": "These are words you hear every time you talk about programming logic and syntax.", "type": "text"}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Exchange information about logic, its principles, and methods in simple spoken and written situations.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands key information in simple written and spoken texts about topics related to software programming and its history. Recognizes basic ideas on programming concepts and programming history in both written and spoken passages.", "type": "secondary_1"}], "type": "objectives"}, {"content": "enpe7n1le01ob05re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Present Continuous Tense in Affirmative Statements", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use the <strong>present continuous</strong> to talk about an action that is happening at the moment of speaking.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "The <strong>present continuous</strong> is used to describe current actions and facts that are currently happening, not at the moment of speaking but nowadays. </br></br>  Let's take a review of the structure of affirmative statements in present continuous, it is as follows: </br></br>  <span class=\"italic\"><center>Subject +<b> verb to be (am, is, are) + verb in gerund (-ing) </b>+ complement </center></br> <br>Example: </br> Jacob is writ<strong>ing</strong> the program's code. </br> They are work<strong>ing</strong> on a new code. </br></br></div></span>  Remember the conjugation of the verb to be , which is used as an auxiliary verb: </br> <span class=\"italic\"> <li>I <b>am arranging </b>syntax. </br> <li>You <b>are encoding</b> symbols. </br> <li>He <b>is creating</b> conditional statements. </br> <li>She <b>is working </b>in the workflow. </br> <li>It <b>is executing </b>if-else statements. </br> <li>We <b>are checking </b>possible variables. </br> <li>They <b>are defining </b>keywords. </br></br></span>  There is a rule to add  -ing suffix at the end of the verb, every time you have a doubt on how to do it, check the following chart:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":5,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"RULE TO ADD -ING \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"COMMON EXAMPLES\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Verb ends in an <span class=\\\"strong\\\">E</span> we remove the <span class=\\\"strong\\\">E</span> and add <span class=\\\"strong\\\">ING.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Take / taking <br>Make/making\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Verb ends in a <span class=\\\"strong\\\">consonant + vowel + consonant</span>, we <span class=\\\"strong\\\">double the final consonant</span> and add ING.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Get / getting <br>Program/ programming<br> Plan / planning\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Do not double the final consonant when the verb ends in <span class=\\\"strong\\\">W, X or Y</span> or when the final syllable is not emphasized.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Fix/ fixing \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Verb ends in <span class=\\\"strong\\\">IE</span> we change it tong <span class=\\\"strong\\\">YING.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Lie/ lying\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "I am working on my project using the correct information.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "When we are programming organization of words and symbols make any programming language usable.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Programmers are always paying attention to logic and syntax.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "When programmers are writing commands such as \u201cprint\u201d, \u201cimport\u201d or \u201cexport\u201d, in fact they are using keywords.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "That is the workflow path which is indicating how the program can skip a part of the code when necessary.", "type": "example"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Comments in Programming", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use <strong>programming comments</strong> to guide yourself in the code you are writing or to help others understand. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "When programmers are writing codes it is very common to find some of them difficult to understand. Some codes can be very confusing for anyone trying to interpret those. In order to avoid errors and clarify the logic of the code, programmers have the option to include a programming comment or an <strong>annotation.</strong></br></br>  A programming comment is included within special characters to avoid confusing this with the code. There are two kinds of comments: the \u2018end of line comment' and the \u2018block comment'. </br></br>  As the name implies an \u2018end of the line' comment comes at the end of a code line, like this: </br></br> <span class=\"italic\"> max = 100;   // using default size. </br></br></span>  A \u2018block comment' has a terminator and it can be very short (less than one line) or very long, using several lines, like this: </br></br>  <span class=\"italic\">/* check input for valid values and print error message for accounting if problems.  */</span>", "type": "text"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "usable ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "available and possibly valuable", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: When we are programming organization of words and symbols make any programming language usable.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n1le01ob05aud01", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "execution path ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a route indicated as a reference to execute a programming code", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: A variable can be a sign or a symbol that stores values like strings, numbers or Boolean values.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n1le01ob05aud02", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "boolean value ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "values with only two possibilities: true or false", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: A variable can be a sign or a symbol that stores values like strings, numbers or Boolean values.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n1le01ob05aud03", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "withdraw ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to take something out of, ask for something, like money", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": " Example: If you go to an ATM machine to withdraw $100 and you have the correct balance\u2026 ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n1le01ob05aud04", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "arrangement ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "an organization and settlement of elements ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Syntax is a set of rules that can indicate the appropriate arrangement of words and symbols.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n1le01ob05aud05", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "balance ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the amount of money in the bank", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: If your balance is less than the requested amount, for sure you will see the message: \u201cinsufficient balance\u201d.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n1le01ob05aud06", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Look for information about the \u201cif-statement\u201d and the \u201cif-else statement\u201d.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Describe how each statement works.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Choose one of the statements and write an example.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Explain the example to your classmates and teacher.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"content": "I look for information about two kinds of statements.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I describe how statements work.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I write examples about statements.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I share statements information and examples.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}]}